Bugfix: Image paths stay correct when one instance is reachable under two web roots

The cache for image paths did not include the web root, although every cached
path starts with it. When the same instance was served under two web roots -
typically "/" without single sign-on and an Apache alias such as "/oc-shib"
protected by Shibboleth - whichever entry point was used first decided the
image paths for both. Pages on the other entry point then loaded images
through the wrong path, e.g. the login background via the SSO alias, which
redirected to the identity provider and was blocked by the Content Security
Policy. The web root is now part of the cache key.
